WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:05.319
The Master of the Mystic Arts may be coming
face to face with an old ally - and it won't

00:00:05.319 --> 00:00:07.060
be a friendly reunion.

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:11.470
Inside sources are reporting that Baron Mordo,
who became thoroughly disillusioned with the

00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:16.119
Ancient One at the end of ​Doctor Strange​,
will be the main antagonist of Doctor Strange

00:00:16.119 --> 00:00:17.119
2.

00:00:17.119 --> 00:00:20.960
Although the casting has yet to be confirmed,
this lines up well with the information we

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:22.240
do have.

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:25.909
Doctor Strange 2 was one of the forthcoming
Marvel flicks reported to be on the way by

00:00:25.909 --> 00:00:31.349
the mysterious Twitter user "Roger Wardell"
in a massive leak earlier this month.

00:00:31.349 --> 00:00:35.590
While we tend to take such things with a grain
of salt, the twitter user has leaked highly

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:37.840
accurate information in the past.

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:42.220
According to sources close to We Got This
Covered, the second solo outing for the good

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:47.059
doctor is in, quote, "deep development," with
the first film's director Scott Derrickson

00:00:47.059 --> 00:00:50.570
and screenwriter C. Robert Cargill already
hard at work.

00:00:50.570 --> 00:00:55.500
According to these sources, when we next see
Mordo, played by Chiwetel Ejiofor, he'll be

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:59.339
in "full-on villain" mode, intent on ridding
the world of magic.

00:00:59.339 --> 00:01:03.449
While the details of Ejiofor's contract aren't
known, it's all but certain that he'll be

00:01:03.449 --> 00:01:07.930
reprising his role given his impressive performance
in the first movie.

00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:12.640
Ejiofor is a brilliant actor, and in Doctor
Strange, he invested Mordo with a strong set

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:17.299
of ideals and a conflicted nature that shone
through despite the character's relatively

00:01:17.299 --> 00:01:19.200
limited screen time.

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:23.610
As we've seen, the MCU's greatest villains
aren't the ones who simply want to cause chaos

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:25.310
and/or rule the universe.

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:29.620
It's characters like Thanos, who enacted a
plan to wipe out half of all life in the universe

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:34.670
for supposedly benevolent reasons, and Loki,
who seems to constantly struggle against his

00:01:34.670 --> 00:01:38.880
own worst impulses, who strike the biggest
chord among Marvel fans.

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:44.020
Mordo began Doctor Strange as a firm disciple
of the Ancient One and her ways, but was shaken

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:48.310
by the fact that she had harnessed power from
the Dark Dimension while forbidding her students

00:01:48.310 --> 00:01:49.780
to do the same.

00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:53.399
His assertion during the film's post-credits
scene speaks to a new worldview:

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:58.000
"Because I see at long last what is wrong
with this world"

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.200
"Too many sorcerors."

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:04.830
His new belief systems seem to be wrapped
up around the belief that to use magic at

00:02:04.830 --> 00:02:09.720
all, even in defense of our entire universe,
is to invite catastrophe upon that universe.

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:14.670
At any rate, assuming the report is accurate,
Mordo is likely to be one of many villains

00:02:14.670 --> 00:02:16.519
in play for Doctor Strange 2.

00:02:16.519 --> 00:02:21.790
A previous leak from "Roger Wardell" has suggested
that the sequel will also take place in the

00:02:21.790 --> 00:02:25.340
1980s and see the introduction of some new
characters.

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:26.340
Wardell wrote,

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:29.180
"Doctor Strange 2: 1980's Boogaloo.

00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:31.980
Tilda Swinton is in talks to return as the
Ancient One.

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:37.409
Jericho Drumm and Clea will make their MCU
debuts, Clea will likely be portrayed by an

00:02:37.409 --> 00:02:38.620
Asian actress.

00:02:38.620 --> 00:02:41.260
Most importantly the gloves will be back!"

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:45.050
We should point out once again that none of
this has been confirmed, but we expect to

00:02:45.050 --> 00:02:49.410
get a lot more information on the MCU's Phase
4 within the next few weeks.

00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:54.140
In July, Marvel will present at San Diego
Comic Con's Hall H, where the studio has made

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:56.700
a ton of significant announcements in the
past.

00:02:56.700 --> 00:03:02.239
However, even Hall H may simply be a warm-up
for a second presentation to follow at Disney's

00:03:02.239 --> 00:03:04.530
D23 expo in August.

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:09.050
It's quite likely that Marvel's entire Phase
4 slate will be revealed at that time, and

00:03:09.050 --> 00:03:13.739
we can finally confirm or debunk the seemingly
never-ending torrent of rumors which have

00:03:13.739 --> 00:03:15.129
been leaking all year.

00:03:15.129 --> 00:03:19.870
We'll be on the lookout for any more leaks,
and we'll keep you up to date.

